th drugs can be administered orally or topically, providing flexibility in treatment. Erythromycin and rovamycin are not recommended for treating BV in pregnancy, as they are not effective for this condition. Proper diagnosis and timely treatment are crucial to mitigate the risks associated with BV during pregnancy, ensuring the health and well-being of both the mother and the fetus.''' \n"], "raw_output": "Option: B", "error": null}
